   "reply": "`python tools/check.py` now passes. The one unit test is OK and there are no line-length violations.\n\nThe only thing it needed was the `NOTES_HOME` environment variable. `tools/check.py` reads it with `os.environ[\"NOTES_HOME\"]` and exited with a `KeyError` when it wasn't set. The variable is the directory where the check harness writes scratch notes. I pointed it at a fresh temp directory:\n\n```\nexport NOTES_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\"; python tools/check.py\n```\n\nI didn't change any code or files in the project. Set `NOTES_HOME` in your shell or CI before running the checks. If you'd rather it work without that, `check.py` could fall back to a temp directory when the variable is missing. I haven't made that change.",
